</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODQ5MDQ1OTYyODUzOTA4NDg=', 'text': "Why @SadhguruJV started the Save Soil movement, Soil is \n\n1. Living Ecosystem: Soil is not mere dirt but a complex, living entity teeming with life. Sadhguru emphasizes that soil hosts 25% of the planet's total biodiversity, making it a critical foundation for life itself.\n\n2. Critical for Human Survival: According to Sadhguru, soil health directly affects human health. It's the source of nourishment, with 95% of our food coming from soil. The degradation of soil could lead to the loss of essential micronutrients, impacting human health dramatically.\n\n3. Climate Change Mitigator: Soil acts as a carbon sink. Conscious Planet highlights that healthy soil can store more carbon than the atmosphere. Degraded soil not only releases CO2 but also loses its ability to mitigate climate change effects.\n\n4. Biodiversity Loss: Sadhguru's initiatives of Save Soil point out that soil degradation has led to the extinction of species, with biodiversity loss in soil being an under-recognized crisis. Soil health is crucial for maintaining ecological balance.\n\n5. Water Cycle: Healthy soil plays a pivotal role in the water cycle, absorbing and holding water. Sadhguru notes that soil degradation leads to decreased water retention, exacerbating droughts and floods.\n\n6. Agricultural Productivity: The Conscious Planet movement stresses that with current practices, we have soil left for only about 60 harvests. This alarming statistic underscores the urgent need for soil conservation to ensure food security.\n\n7. Global Degradation: Over 52% of agricultural land worldwide is already degraded, according to Sadhguru's campaigns. This degradation not only threatens food production but also the livelihoods of billions dependent on agriculture.\n\n8. Economic Impact: The loss of soil health has a direct economic impact. Sadhguru and Conscious Planet argue that soil degradation costs billions in lost productivity, increased health costs due to poor nutrition, and disaster management from altered weather patterns.\n\n9. Policy and Awareness: Sadhguru has advocated for soil to become an election issue globally, pushing for policies that mandate at least 3-6% organic content in soil to maintain its health. Public awareness is seen as key to driving change.\n\n10. A Call to Action: The Save Soil movement, supported by Sadhguru, is a call for individuals, communities, and nations to act now. It's not just about saving soil for agriculture but preserving the very foundation of life on Earth. The movement has reached millions, showing the global resonance of this cause.\n\nHappy to read the news!", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '67611162', 'name': 'Sadhguru', 'screen_name': 'SadhguruJV', 'indices': [4, 15]}]}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 9, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 30 10:00:50 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1884683140448522597', 'display_text_range': [14, 291], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}, {'id_str': '67611162', 'name': 'Sadhguru', 'screen_name': 'SadhguruJV', 'indices': [18, 29]}]}, 'favorite_count': 126, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd Why @SadhguruJV started the Save Soil movement, Soil is \n\n1. Living Ecosystem: Soil is not mere dirt but a complex, living entity teeming with life. Sadhguru emphasizes that soil hosts 25% of the planet's total biodiversity, making it a critical foundation for life itself.\n\n2.", 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1884683140448522597', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 2, 'reply_count': 4, 'retweet_count': 47, 'retweeted': False